    {
      "id": 233548,
      "name": "Escher",
      "username": "Escher",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/escher/{size}/4865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-08-30T00:01:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Kid Radical\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Kid Radical:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I had been wondering what his whole deal was for the first 20 years or so of his existence, since he started early 50s while both phenomea he nods to (Kung-Fu stuff and Blaxploitation) are so early 70s.</p>\n<p>The “Joe Lewis but punches crime” idea is era appropriate, neat to think about, but also makes sense as not having quite enough “there” there to get the character to break out or prevent him from being radically overhauled.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This.  When they first backtracked on the dates due to their issue numbers being vastly wrong, I was like “But he’s OBVIOUSLY from the 70s???”  This story resolves the issue.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
